ouble to 256-bit and entirely new post-quantum algorithms to replace RSA. Crypto agility is the architectural approach to address this: instead of hardcoding cryptographic implementations throughout codebases, centralize them behind abstraction layers so algorithms can be swapped without disrupting systems. The practical path involves discovery (building a cryptographic bill of materials), evaluating weak or deprecated instances, prioritizing remediation, and refactoring toward modular, agile crypto design while updating for the quantum era.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ZrHKwxasXS4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T11:00:58.000Z"},{"id":"ck7W91brJ","title":"Claude Security\u2019s public beta, OpenAI\u2019s five-point plan and cybersecurity\u2019s Y2K moment","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EJg67cLfLYo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/claude-security-s-public-beta-openai-s-five-point-plan-and-cybersecurity-s-y2k-moment-ck7w91brj","summary":"IBM's Security Intelligence podcast covers three major cybersecurity stories: Anthropic's Claude Security public beta for enterprise code scanning, OpenAI's five-point AI cyber defense plan, and CrowdStrike's 'QuiltWorks' coalition (including IBM and OpenAI) addressing AI-discovered vulnerabilities. Panelists debate whether this represents cybersecurity's 'Y2K moment,' discuss the Coalition for Secure AI's framework for AI agent identity and access control (proposing zero-trust-style short-lived tokens and role-based access for agents), and analyze CopyFail (CVE-2026-31431), a nearly decade-old Linux privilege escalation flaw affecting all major distros since 2017 that leaves no forensic evidence and requires only a 732-byte Python script to exploit.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EJg67cLfLYo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T10:00:31.000Z"},{"id":"6sb3dE6KN","title":"RAG's Evolution: From Simple Retrieval to Agentic AI","u